Falsifies `elf::verification::check_segment_bounds_never_panics`.

The defect: the file-range addition is trusted rather than checked, `p_offset + filesz` in place
of `checked_add`. The `end > file_len` test two lines down reads as though it covers this, which
is the trap: it catches every value that does not wrap and none of the ones that do.

Expected to fail: the totality claim, as an arithmetic overflow, on a program header naming a
huge offset and a huge size. Both numbers come from a file the kernel was handed, so this is a
crafted binary halting the loader rather than being refused by it.

diff --git a/crates/elf/src/lib.rs b/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/elf/src/lib.rs
@@ -577,5 +577,3 @@ fn check_segment_bounds(
     // checked rather than trusted.
-    let end = p_offset
-        .checked_add(filesz)
-        .ok_or(Error::SegmentOutOfBounds)?;
+    let end = p_offset + filesz;
     if end > file_len {
